--TEST--
`rule:core-classes/db-connection-is-named` memoizes a connection and not a name, so a `Core\Db::connect` after that connection's `close` answers a usable handle again — while the closed handle stays closed and stays refused — `rule:core-classes/db-connection-is-named` and `rule:security/db-pool-reset-is-a-boundary` and spec § 18
--FILE--
<?nvs
// covers: Core\Db\Connection::close
// § 2: two `connect("main")` calls in one request are one connection, so the
// second call below is only reached because the first connection has been
// released — a name whose connection has gone is a name the memo no longer
// answers for.
var $first = Core\Db::connect("main");
$first->execute("create table t (id integer primary key)", []);
$first->close();
echo "first: ", $first->isOpen() ? "open" : "closed", "\n";

var $second = Core\Db::connect("main");
echo "second: ", $second->isOpen() ? "open" : "closed", "\n";
echo "second driver ", $second->driver() == Core\Db\Driver::Sqlite ? "is sqlite" : "is something else", "\n";

// The new handle is usable, which is the half `isOpen()` alone does not say:
// a statement runs on it.
var $wrote = $second->execute("insert into t (id) values (?)", [1]);
echo "second wrote ", $wrote->affected(), "\n";

// **This case deliberately asserts nothing about which connection that is.**
// § 13 releases a `close`d connection to this core's pool, so the second
// `connect` may well be handed the very one the first gave up — pooling is
// exactly that, and a case pinning "a different database" would be pinning the
// absence of the pool.
//
// What it does assert is that the two *handles* are separate: closing one is
// not a statement about the block, and the closed one is still refused.
try {
    $first->query("select id from t", []);
    echo "first: not refused\n";
} catch (LogicError $refused) {
    echo "first: still refused\n";
}
echo "first still: ", $first->isOpen() ? "open" : "closed", "\n";
$second->close();
--FILE nvs.toml--
# § 3: `db.connect` covers a SQLite block, whose path is configuration.
[capabilities.db]
connect = ["main"]

[db.main]
driver = "sqlite"
path = ":memory:"
--EXPECT--
first: closed
second: open
second driver is sqlite
second wrote 1
first: still refused
first still: closed
